	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Analog Devices / Maxim MAX17048G+T10, package code T822+3 (8-pin TDFN-EP, 2 x 2 mm, 0.5 mm pitch, exposed pad). Geometry taken verbatim from the Maxim RECOMMENDED PACKAGE LAND PATTERN drawing, DOCUMENT CONTROL NO. 90-0065, REV. E, sheet 1/1, titled 'PACKAGE LAND PATTERN, 8L TDFN, 2X2 MM'. Applicability is established by the MAX17048/MAX17049 datasheet package table, which maps PACKAGE TYPE T822+3 to OUTLINE NO. 21-0168 and LAND PATTERN NO. 90-0065. Drawing dimensions used: signal land 0.70 (x) x 0.30 (y); pitch 0.50; pad row centre-to-centre 1.98, so x = +/-0.99 and y = +/-0.25, +/-0.75; exposed pad 0.80 (x) x 1.38 (y). Drawing tolerance is +/-0.02 mm and note 2 states the land pattern complies to IPC7351A. The drawing is marked NOT TO SCALE, so the six printed dimensions were used directly; they were additionally cross-checked against the drawing's own vector geometry, where a single uniform scale of 0.04664 mm/unit reproduces all six labels to within 0.37 percent, confirming which feature each dimension attaches to. REJECTED ALTERNATIVE - the stock KiCad footprint Package_DFN_QFN:TDFN-8-1EP_2x2mm_P0.5mm_EP0.8x1.2mm cites the same Maxim outline 21-0168 but does NOT match this land pattern: its exposed pad is 0.80 x 1.20 against Maxim's 0.80 x 1.38 (0.18 mm short, a 13 percent area deficit) and its signal land is 0.25 wide against Maxim's 0.30 (0.05 mm NARROWER, which is a reduction and therefore cannot be an IPC fillet expansion). It corresponds to a different T822 exposed-pad variant and was not used. PROJECT DECISIONS, not manufacturer geometry - (a) signal lands are drawn as roundrect with rratio 0.25 for manufacturability; the land envelope is exactly Maxim's 0.70 x 0.30 and only the corners are relieved. (b) 90-0065 gives NO solder-mask guidance, so all lands are non-solder-mask-defined at KiCad's default mask expansion. (c) 90-0065 gives NO paste guidance, so the exposed pad is printed through four apertures of 0.34 x 0.62 at (+/-0.23, +/-0.38), flush with the pad boundary and separated by 0.12 mm in x and 0.14 mm in y, giving 0.843 mm2 of 1.104 mm2 or 76 percent coverage, which sits inside the IPC-7093 band for exposed pads; this mirrors the segmentation idiom already used for U9 in this library. (d) 90-0065 specifies NO thermal vias, so none are included; vias under the exposed pad remain a PCB-layout task. Pin 1 is top-left in top view with numbering running counter-clockwise: 1-4 down the left flank, 5-8 up the right flank.")
	(tags "Maxim ADI MAX17048 MAX17049 T822 TDFN-8 TDFN 2x2 0.5mm exposed-pad fuel-gauge 90-0065 21-0168")
